    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d463">

                <pb facs="0480" n="1214" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1214"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Uhl to Mr.
                            Taylor.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-10-23"><hi rendition="#italic">October 23,
                        1895</hi>.</date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 419.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I append on the overleaf a copy of your
                    telegram of the 21st instant, to the effect that the Spanish Government was
                    disposed to grant at once to consuls of this Government in Cuba all rights
                    guaranteed to German consuls under the treaty of 1870.</p>
                <p>Mr. Olney’s note to Mr. Dupuy de Lôme, of the 11th instant,<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d463-f1"/> answers his communication in the sense indicated by the
                    minister of state and thus anticipated his excellency’s gratifying
                    assurances.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwin F. Uhl</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
